+ * locker, S the granted ones, U the unlocks. A waiter enters with its own L
+ * (ordinal). When U reaches S with kernel bits set, userland sets L to
+ * count|K, marks S unset (IBIT) and calls rw_unlock with S = U: the kernel
+ * grants the waiter with ordinal S + 1 (in INC units), a writer alone or a
+ * run of consecutive readers present in the kernel, and every granted thread
+ * returns updatebits = n * INC | bits (writer K|E; W|K kept while ordinals
+ * up to the highest L seen are still waiting); the first one adds n to S in
